Both of the leading AI labs have experienced serious loss of control incidents. These are complex, emergent events that were detected weeks after they occurred, and there will be significant efforts to address them.

@AnthropicAI reports that during cybersecurity reviews, three incidents were found where a Claude model reached the internet from within or during interaction with a third-party evaluation environment, gaining unauthorized access to the systems of three organizations. They describe what happened, how it occurred, and the changes they are implementing. They also encourage other AI developers to conduct similar reviews.

This collaboration with evaluation partners like @Irregular highlights the importance of joint efforts in ensuring the security and safety of AI systems.
